action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P92 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): what a click in the text field does, then text
# selected by dragging and copied. The field starts as "hello", focused with its text selected.
# CLICK: a click right of the text, then X typed: "X" if a click selects everything, "helloX" if it
# places the caret. Command-Z puts "hello" back.
# DRAG: pressed at the start of "hello" (frame x 86 -- GTK insets the text 4 points more than AppKit)
# and moved right 5 points at a time to x 121 past its end, then let go. Command-C copies, the right
# arrow moves the caret to the end, Command-V pastes: "hellohello".
# Expected "field" lines in p92-commands.log, in order: helloX | hello | hellohello.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P92:點擊文字欄位的行為，以及拖曳選取再複製。GTK 的文字內距比 AppKit 多 4 點，所以從 x 86 按下。
# p92-commands.log 的 field 各行應依序為 helloX、hello、hellohello。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let the window settle,macos
click,250,167,frame,left,,,CLICK: right of the text in the field,macos
sleep,,,,,,400000,,macos
key,,,,,x,,type x,macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
keydown,,,,,command,,,macos
key,,,,,z,,undo the x,macos
keyup,,,,,command,,,macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
mousedown,86,167,frame,left,,,DRAG: press at the start of hello,macos
sleep,,,,,,100000,,macos
